\import{fdip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Remark}
\title{Finite sign counts and two infinite-volume comparisons}
\date{2026-11-21}

\p{On the free sign orbit, \ref{fdip-0124} specializes to the
equality #{Z=16\check Z} of \ref{fdip-0125}, an equality of finite
sums on the torus with #{4} vertices. Wegner's changed-coupling
discussion is in
\citet{Section 7.1, pp. 15–16, Equations (66)–(68)}{wegner2014duality}.
The fixed-length sign model of
\citet{authors’ preprint, §II, pp. 17–19, (2.15)}{fradkin1979higgs}
is the comparison recorded in \ref{fdip-0118}. Both of those
discussions use infinite volume.}
